# apps/web and apps/mobile — platform shells

## Routes must stay thin

```tsx
'use client'; // web only, when re-exporting shared screens
export { LoginScreen as default } from '@project-template/app';
```

Do not add screen UI, forms, or business logic in route files.

## What belongs in apps (platform-specific)

- **Web:** `providers.tsx`, `lib/auth.tsx`, `lib/convex-client.ts`, OAuth pages (`/auth/google`, `/auth/apple`), API routes, `next.config.mjs`
- **Mobile:** `_layout.tsx`, `lib/auth.tsx`, `lib/convex.ts`, `app/auth/callback.tsx`

## Auth wiring pattern

Apps create `AuthProvider` by calling `createAuthProvider(api, tokenStore)` from `@project-template/app` with the platform token store, then wrap the tree in `_layout` / `providers.tsx`.

## Web + react-native-web

- Shared screens transpile via `next.config.mjs` (`transpilePackages`, `react-native-web` alias).
- Do not import `@project-template/ui` or `@project-template/app` in Server Components without a `'use client'` boundary.
